WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.490
Will the Pryde of the X-Men ever make it back
to the big screen?

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:06.940
Or have plans for a Kitty Pryde feature officially
fallen through the floor?

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.660
In a recent sitdown with ComicBook, Deadpool
director Tim Miller discussed the long-awaited

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:16.000
solo feature for fan favorite mutant Kitty
Pryde, which he had been developing before

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.720
Fox Studios' acquisition by Disney earlier
this year.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:22.080
His comments were, we're sorry to report,
not encouraging.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.860
Before the much-ballyhooed merger, Miller
had been all set to direct the flick from

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.440
a script by comics legend Brian Michael Bendis.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:32.790
Pryde has been a Marvel mainstay for nearly
40 years; with her ability to phase through

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:37.280
solid matter and her quirky, sardonic sense
of humor, she quickly endeared herself to

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.300
readers, helping to propel sales of X-Men
comics into the stratosphere in the '80s.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.640
The character seems like she would have been
a fine fit for Miller, who did an excellent

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:48.940
job of bringing Deadpool's ass-kicking, profanely
humorous aesthetic to the screen in the Merc

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.400
with a Mouth's first solo outing.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:54.840
Likewise, it would have been fascinating to
see Bendis' big-screen take on the character;

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:59.440
among the many heroes he's created for Marvel
over the years is Jessica Jones, a tough,

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.879
complex female character who translated well
to live-action in her unfortunately canceled

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:04.900
Netflix series.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:10.040
But unfortunately, Miller has confirmed what
many fans anticipated: the Kitty Pryde project

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.060
is dead in the water.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.000
Miller said,

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.240
"I love the X-Men.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.780
I don't expect Marvel to call me and say,
'Come do the X-Men,' so I'm not waiting for

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:17.280
that.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.760
I was really excited about my Kitty Pryde
movie.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.120
[...] It'll never happen now."

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.240
"The X-Men don't have room for whiny brats!"

00:01:24.249 --> 00:01:26.259
"Just who are you calling whiny?

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:27.020
I'll show you!

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:27.520
I'll —"

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.340
"Hold it, Kitty."

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.600
Miller's comments are a pretty radical departure
from Bendis' response when he was asked for

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.800
an update on the project this past February.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:39.140
In response to a fan query on Twitter, Bendis
said that he was working on the script at

00:01:39.149 --> 00:01:42.959
that time, failing to even make mention of
the impending acquisition of the studio which

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.000
had greenlit the film.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:48.060
Alas, things seem to have taken a significant
turn for the worse for the project in the

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:51.889
intervening months, and that's not all the
bad news that Miller has had to endure as

00:01:51.889 --> 00:01:52.400
of late.

00:01:52.889 --> 00:01:57.239
His second feature directorial effort, Terminator:
Dark Fate, flopped mightily at the box office

00:01:57.239 --> 00:02:02.239
despite relatively solid reviews, making it
another franchise that probably won't be coming

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.460
back anytime soon.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.200
We're of the opinion, though, that the helmer
shouldn't be quite so pessimistic.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:12.220
Deadpool was a rousing success, single-handedly
proving that R-rated superhero pictures were

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:15.720
viable in today's age of non-stop PG-13 blockbusters.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:19.360
It remains to be seen if Disney will bring
him into the fold to put his talents to use

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.360
with a new Marvel property — but it'd probably
be a good idea to reach out.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:27.680
While nothing is official yet, all signs are
indicating that Marvel Studios will eventually

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.460
give the greenlight to a third Deadpool movie
at some point in the near future.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.720
Star Ryan Reynolds, who was born to play the
role, has openly expressed his hope that the

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:39.590
three-quel will get the green light sooner
rather than later, and the writers of the

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:43.460
first two installments, Rhett Reese and Paul
Wernick, are confident that it's just a matter

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.520
of time before the flick is put into production.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:49.960
For that matter, Marvel Studios' brass have
indicated that they expect to eventually recast

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:54.870
every member of the X-Men except Deadpool,
and Disney CEO Bob Iger has publicly said

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.700
that the Mouse House would be just fine with
Marvel making an R-rated superhero film.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:03.520
Add to this the fact that Reynolds was recently
seen popping by Marvel Studios' offices for

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:08.210
a visit, and it all adds up the strong possibility
that we'll get some news about Deadpool 3

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:09.100
before too long.

00:03:09.629 --> 00:03:13.400
Other than a potential third outing for Deadpool,
though, it looks like every single one of

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.660
the Marvel-related projects that were in development
at Fox before the merger are dying on the

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:18.160
vine.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:22.320
The Channing Tatum-starring Gambit, in development
for the better part of a decade, recently

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.140
received a vote of no-confidence from formerly
attached director Doug Liman;

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:30.720
Logan director James Mangold has said that
a planned spin-off featuring Dafne Keen's

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:35.910
X-23 is unlikely to happen, and James Franco's
Multiple Man failed to reach a significant

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:40.280
stage of development before the merger, meaning
that it, too, is almost certainly done for.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:42.980
"So good."

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.640
It simply makes more sense for Marvel Studios
to develop these characters for the screen

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:51.760
in their own inimitable fashion rather than
to continue on the course that Fox was plotting

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:56.520
— especially after the critical and commercial
failure of the final Fox-produced X-Men film,

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.340
Dark Phoenix.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:02.220
Having said that, a Miller-directed, Bendis-scripted
Kitty Pryde flick sounds like something we

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:06.680
would want to see, and if Marvel head honcho
Kevin Feige has any designs on introducing

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:11.180
the character into the MCU, he could do worse
than to bring the pair in for a chat.

